<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Spec 31 §3/§5: the macOS runtime signing profile (fixed pair, pinned
  here until spec 31 §2's manifest derivation lands).

  disable-library-validation — EVERY runtime slice: a hardened-runtime
    process by default refuses unsigned dylibs, and the driver's boot
    arms DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES with the in-image preload shim (spec 22
    tier 1 — the unpatched R interpreter's only VFS visibility); the
    shim carries no Developer ID signature of its own (§1.4). The same
    grant covers the driver materializing in-image native objects
    (the lapack module, libRlapack/libRblas, the preload shim) to the
    host for dlopen.
  allow-jit — a grant, never a requirement: R has no JIT surface (the
    byte compiler is an ahead-of-time serializer), so the entitlement
    is inert today; it rides the pair so the profile never needs a
    re-review if a JIT-bearing interpreter configuration arrives.

  Keep the two <true/> values on their own lines: the embedding check
  in ci/macos-sign-notarize-runtime.sh counts them (macOS 15 emits the
  embedded plist single-line, so it greps for <true/>, not key names).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
